PLAN WITH FRIENDS PRD - Michelle & Mara
Product Requirements Document: New Feature

Build name:  Plan with Friends
Owner:  Michelle Sainsbury & Mara Munoz
Date:  9/28/2026


1. PROBLEM
Eventbrite users who discover events they may want to attend with friends have no built-in way to coordinate interest or availability before registering. Because that decision-making happens outside of Eventbrite through texts, group chats, or other apps, users must leave the event experience to determine whether their group wants to attend. This creates friction between discovering an event and committing to registration.
Supporting Context (optional)

Eventbrite currently allows users to discover event details and register for events, but it does not provide a shared space for friends to coordinate interest or availability before registering.
Users planning to attend an event together may need to leave Eventbrite and use texts, group chats, or other communication tools to decide who wants to attend.
This creates a gap between discovering an event and committing to registration because the group-planning portion of the journey happens outside the Eventbrite experience.

1a. Opportunity

Plan with Friends creates an opportunity to keep users within the Eventbrite experience while they coordinate whether to attend an event together. By making group interest and availability visible before registration, Eventbrite can reduce friction between discovering an event and committing to attend.

Market Opportunity

According to Eventbrite’s 2026 Social Study, 79% of 18–35-year-olds surveyed in the U.S. and U.K. planned to attend more events in 2026. The study surveyed 4,051 people ages 18–35 in July 2025, demonstrating strong interest in live-event attendance among younger adults. (Eventbrite, 2026)
A 2020 study of adolescent music-event attendance found that 94% of respondents reported attending gigs or concerts with close friends, while 19% reported attending alone, demonstrating the social role that friends can play in live-event attendance.
(Sustainability, 2020)

Eventbrite’s 2026 Social Study also found that 69% of respondents rely on personal networks and word-of-mouth to discover experiences, providing additional support for integrating social decision-making into the event experience. (Eventbrite, 2026)

1b. Users & Needs

Primary user(s):  Eventbrite users who discover events they are interested in attending with friends but want to know whether their friends are interested and available before registering.

Secondary users:  Friends invited to a Plan with Friends group who need a quick, simple way to review the event and communicate whether they are interested and available without having to register first.

Key User Needs
As an Eventbrite user, I need to invite friends to consider an event with me because I may not want to commit to attending until I know who else is interested.

As an Eventbrite user, I need to see my friends’ interest and availability in one place because coordinating across separate text messages or group chats makes the decision harder to track.

As an invited friend, I need to quickly review the event and respond to the invitation because I want to participate in the group decision without having to register first.

As an Eventbrite user, I need a clear path from group planning to registration because once my group decides to attend, I want to continue without restarting the event-discovery process.

1c. Current User Journey
1. User browses Eventbrite and discovers an event they may want to attend with friends.
2. User opens the event details page to review the event.
→ Problem: The user has no shared planning space within the event experience to determine whether friends are interested and available.
3. User leaves Eventbrite and contacts friends through texts, group chats, or another communication app.
→ Problem: Responses are scattered across another platform, separating group decision-making from the event itself.
4. User determines whether the group wants to attend and returns to Eventbrite to register.
→ Problem: The user must re-enter the Eventbrite experience after coordinating elsewhere before completing registration.


2. PROPOSED SOLUTION

Plan with Friends is a new Eventbrite planning experience that allows users to coordinate with friends before committing to an event. From an event they are considering, users can create a shared plan, invite friends, and see whether the group is interested and available to attend. Once the group is ready to move forward, users can continue from the shared plan toward event registration. As a result, users can make group attendance decisions without moving the planning process to separate text messages or group chats.

2a. Value Proposition

Eventbrite users who want to attend events with friends but struggle to coordinate interest and availability before registering can use Plan with Friends to make that decision together within the event experience. Unlike coordinating through separate texts or group chats, Plan with Friends provides one shared space to invite friends, view responses, and move directly toward registration once the group is ready.

2b. Top 3 MVP Value Props

The Vitamin  (must-have baseline):  Users can create a shared plan for an event, invite friends, and view their responses in one place.

The Painkiller  (solves the core pain):  Users can coordinate interest and availability without leaving the event experience for separate texts or group chats.

The Steroid  (the magic moment):  Users can see the group’s responses together and move directly from deciding as a group toward event registration.

2c. Goals & Non-Goals

Goals
Reduce the friction users experience when coordinating with friends before committing to an event.
Keep group event-planning decisions connected to the Eventbrite experience rather than requiring users to coordinate across separate platforms.
Help users understand their group’s interest and availability before deciding whether to register.
Create a clear transition from group decision-making to event registration.

Non-Goals
Build a full messaging, group-chat, or social networking platform; the MVP is focused specifically on pre-registration event coordination.
Replace Eventbrite’s existing registration and ticketing experience; Plan with Friends leads users back into the existing registration flow.
Build advanced scheduling, calendar coordination, or event-recommendation tools; these are outside the scope of this MVP.

