3. REQUIREMENTS
User Journey 1: Event attendee creates a plan with friends

Context:  An Eventbrite user finds an event they may want to attend with friends and wants to coordinate the group’s interest and availability before committing to registration.


Sub-journey 1: Starting a Plan with Friends
[P0]  User can start a Plan with Friends from the event details page.
[P0]  User can create a plan that is connected to the selected event.
[P0]  User can view the event name, date, time, and location within the plan.
[P0] User can view available group discount information within the plan.
[P1]  User can return from the planning space to the full event details.
[P2]  User can add a short note to the group when creating the plan.

Sub-journey 2: Inviting Friends
[P0]  User can add friends to the event plan.
[P0]  User can generate or share an invitation that allows friends to access the plan.
[P1]  User can see which friends have been invited.
[P1]  User can see which invited friends have responded.
[P2]  User can resend an invitation to a friend who has not responded.

Sub-journey 3: Reviewing responses and deciding to attend
[P0]  User can view each friend’s interest response in the shared plan.
[P0]  User can view each friend’s availability response.
[P0]  User can continue from the group plan toward event registration.
[P1]  User can see a summary of the group’s responses.

User Journey 2: Invited friend responds to an event plan

Context:  A friend receives an invitation to consider an event and needs a quick way to understand the event, indicate whether they are interested and available, and participate in the group decision before registering.

Sub-journey 1: Reviewing the invitation
[P0]  User can open the shared Plan with Friends invitation.
[P0]  User can view the event name, date, time, and location before responding.
[P1]  User can view who invited them to the plan.
[P1]  User can access the full event details if they need more information.
[P2]  User can view which other friends have been invited.

Sub-journey 2: Responding to the plan
[P0]  User can indicate whether they are interested in attending the event.
[P0]  User can indicate whether they are available for the event date and time.
[P1]  User can change their response after submitting it.
[P1]  User can view the group's current responses after responding.


4. APPENDIX

Supporting Research

Eventbrite’s 2026 Social Study reported that 79% of 18–35-year-olds planned to attend more events in 2026, supporting continued demand for in-person event experiences. (EventBrite)

Research on live music attendance found that 94% of respondents reported attending gigs/concerts with close friends, supporting the importance of social relationships in event attendance. (MDPI)

Additional qualitative research found that attending with friends can encourage commitment and that people use messaging groups to coordinate event plans.

